{"name":"Beyond the Wall","hex":"#d7e0eb","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"beyond","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Preposition","definitions":["Further away than.","On the far side of."]},{"part":"Adverb","definitions":["Farther along or away.","In addition; more."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/beyond"},{"term":"wall","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A rampart of earth, stones etc. built up for defensive purposes.","A structure built for defense surrounding a city, castle etc."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To enclose with, or as if with, a wall or walls.","To use a wallhack."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/wall"}],"entries":[{"title":"Beyond the Wall (EP)","blocks":[{"text":"Beyond the Wall is an EP by the German heavy metal band Rage, released in 1992. The songs \"Bury All Life\" and \"I Want You\" were taken for bonus tracks for the Trapped!'s 2002 remaster, and the songs \"On the Edge\", \"Dust\" and \"The Body Talks\" for Execution Guaranteed's 2002 remaster."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/1/18/Ragebeyondthewallcover.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Beyond_the_Wall_(EP)","wikidata":"Q4900204"},{"title":"Beyond the Wall (album)","blocks":[{"text":"Beyond the Wall is the twelfth studio album by Kenny Garrett released on August 29, 2006, by Nonesuch Records. Among the musicians on the album are tenor saxophonist Pharoah Sanders, vibraphonist Bobby Hutcherson, pianist Mulgrew Miller, and drummer Brian Blade."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/4/4d/KennyGarrettBeyondTheWallAlbumCover.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Beyond_the_Wall_(album)","wikidata":"Q2900477"},{"title":"Beyond the Wall (Game of Thrones)","blocks":[{"text":"\"Beyond the Wall\" is the sixth and penultimate episode of the seventh season of HBO's fantasy television series Game of Thrones, and the 66th overall. It was written by series co-creators David Benioff and D. B. Weiss, and directed by Alan Taylor. The episode was 70 minutes long, making it one of the longest episodes of the series."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Beyond_the_Wall_(Game_of_Thrones)","wikidata":"Q37577012"},{"title":"Wall","blocks":[{"text":"A wall is a structure and a surface that defines an area; carries a load; provides security, shelter, or soundproofing; or serves a decorative purpose. There are various types of walls, including border barriers between countries, brick walls, defensive walls in fortifications, and retaining walls that hold back dirt, stone, water, or noise. Walls can also be found in buildings, where they support roofs, floors, and ceilings, enclose spaces, and provide shelter and security."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/81/Noel_2005_P%C3%A9kin_031_muraille_de_chine_Mutianyu.jpg/330px-Noel_2005_P%C3%A9kin_031_muraille_de_chine_Mutianyu.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wall","wikidata":"Q42948"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/ba/D._B._Weiss_and_David_Benioff.jpg/500px-D._B._Weiss_and_David_Benioff.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/ba/D._B._Weiss_and_David_Benioff.jpg/500px-D._B._Weiss_and_David_Benioff.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The episode was written by series co-creators David Benioff and D. B. Weiss.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AD._B._Weiss_and_David_Benioff.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/54/Alan_Taylor_2013_crop.jpg/330px-Alan_Taylor_2013_crop.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=th